course: dictionary
lesson: 11444
title: Adherence: sticking to the rules
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adherence means sticking closely to a rule, plan, belief or agreement and following it. It comes from the verb «adhere», which means to stick to something.
explain: «Strict adherence to the school code keeps the corridors calm.» Strict means very exact, so the school code is followed every time, not just sometimes. The words strict adherence tell you the rules are being kept carefully.
explain: Adherence can also mean physically sticking to something: «The tape has good adherence, so the poster stays up.» The clue is stays up. The tape is holding on firmly, so its adherence is good.
fact: Adherence is a noun meaning sticking closely to a rule, plan, belief or agreement.
fact: Adherence is uncountable, so we say good adherence, not an adherence.
fact: Common phrases are adherence to a rule, adherence to a plan and strict adherence.
fact: In health news, adherence means taking medicine exactly as a doctor has said.
fact: Adherence can also mean physical sticking, like glue or tape holding firmly to a surface.
exercise: «Her doctor praised her adherence to the medicine plan.» What does adherence mean here? | Arguing with the doctor | Writing a new plan | Forgetting the plan | *Following the plan closely
exercise: «The tape has good adherence, so the poster stays up.» What does adherence mean in this sentence? | Being very loud | *Sticking firmly to the wall | Being sad about the poster | Reading the poster aloud
exercise: Which word is the noun for sticking closely to a rule? | adhere | admire | *adherence | adjust
test: «Strict adherence to the school code keeps the corridors calm.» Which phrase is closest in meaning to strict adherence? | Quick running | Lazy forgetting | *Careful following | Loud shouting
test: Ben says, «Adherence is when you break a rule.» Is Ben right? | Yes, adherence means breaking rules | Yes, it means the rules are very long | No, adherence means following a rule | *No, adherence means following a rule, not breaking it
exam: Choose the right word: The coach praised the team's ___ to the training plan. | *adherence | silence | sadness | pattern
